# Command Rules
- `justfile` at the project root is the single list of project commands. Run every check through its recipe, never by retyping the command behind it: `just test`, `just property`, `just acceptance`, `just coverage`, `just crap`, `just dry`, `just mutate`, `just gherkin-mutate`, `just docs`, and `just check` for the standard suite.
- Recipe names are fixed across projects; only their bodies change. Do not rename or remove a recipe.
- Keep the recipes for the checks you own correct, in your own commit: the coder owns `test` and `acceptance`; the refactorer owns `property`, `coverage`, `crap`, and `dry`; the architect owns `mutate`, `gherkin-mutate`, and `docs`.
- A recipe that exits with "not wired yet" is its owner's to define when that owner builds what it runs. Any other role that finds a recipe missing or wrong reports it in its handoff instead of editing it.
- Recipes stay non-interactive and run one at a time.
